Krita Nova 15 - floating vertical Brush Panel (Android)

On Android the top bar holds New / Open / Save plus mirror/wrap, layouts and
workspaces. Undo/Redo and the rest of the "Brushes and Stuff" toolbar
(gradient, pattern, colors, brush editor, presets, blending mode, alpha
lock/reload, size, opacity) move into a floating narrow "Brush Panel".

1. KisMainWindow: createAndroidBrushPanel() adds a QDockWidget
   (objectName KritaNovaBrushPanel, Krita's dock title bar) and reparents the
   XMLGUI toolbars "editToolBar" and "BrushesAndStuff" into it, vertical and
   not movable. They stay the same XMLGUI-managed KisToolBar objects, so
   Configure Toolbars keeps working. QMainWindow::restoreState() (window
   settings, workspaces) puts known toolbars back into its toolbar layout
   without reparenting them, which left them invisible in the panel and kept
   the top bar from stretching; an event filter (ParentChange, Move, explicit
   Hide) and the panel's start-up checks take them out of the main window's
   layout again. The dock has no allowed dock areas, is re-floated when
   something docks it, and has no keyboard accelerator in its title. Its
   title bar is a plain grip (Krita's docker title bar has float/dock and
   lock buttons, which could dock or lock it with no way back).
   Like the dockers, the panel is hidden on the welcome page and shown once
   an image is open (follows the main window's widget stack).
   Bringing it back after hiding it: Settings > Toolbars Shown > Brush Panel,
   or switching on "Edit" / "Brushes and Stuff" there, shows it floating and
   on screen again.
2. BrushPanelShower shows the panel 400 ms after the main window is first
   shown (a floating dock is a window of its own and is not shown along with
   the main window; startup's window state / workspace restore may also hide
   or re-dock it). The first time, or whenever it is off screen, it floats at
   the left edge (kritarc: androidBrushPanelPlaced3); otherwise it is
   shown where it was. Settings > Toolbars Shown > Brush Panel hides it for
   the session and brings it back.
3. KisToolBar::mainWindow() searches all ancestors for the main window, not
   just the direct parent; several code paths dereference it unchecked
   (context menu, saveState) and would crash for a toolbar in the panel.

4. Panel layout, centered: a grip to drag it by (no title, no close
   button), Undo, Redo (the "editToolBar"), a "more" button (3 dots), tall
   vertical Size and Opacity sliders, the foreground/background color squares
   (the "dual" action, taken out of the brush toolbar), the color sampler
   button. The more button (KisPopupButton, no title bar, no box border)
   opens one row: the rest of the brush toolbar as a normal horizontal
   toolbar (gradient, pattern, brush editor, presets, blending mode, alpha
   lock, reload), a separator and a close button.
   The sliders (NovaVerticalSlider, 45 px wide) are bound to the same
   KisDoubleSliderSpinBox objects as the hidden horizontal sliders
   (brushslider1/2): drag up/down to change the value relative to where the
   drag started (Size uses the same cubic curve); the value shows while
   dragging. First placement: as narrow as the sliders allow (~52 px), 66% of
   the window height, vertically centered at the left edge (kritarc:
   androidBrushPanelPlaced4). Thin frame (PM_DockWidgetFrameWidth 3 for this
   panel, 3 px side margins, extra room around the color squares/sampler).
   The "more" popup closes on any press outside it, including pen/touch on
   the canvas (Qt only does that for mouse presses), and the 3-dot button's
   pressed/hover highlight is cleared when it closes (MorePopupCloser).
   The panel and the "more" popup have rounded corners (8 px) and a grey
   1.5 px outline: translucent window background, painted by
   RoundedPanelPainter (an event filter) instead of the widget's own
   background and frame. The popup is a frameless window (no white Android
   platform frame).
5. Top row: the main toolbar (mainToolBar) moves from the toolbar area into
   a fixed, title-less dock in the top dock area ("KritaNovaTopBar"; same
   keeper as the panel toolbars). Toolbar areas and dock areas never share a
   row, dock widgets do: once after startup, a Toolbox docker docked at the
   top is split onto the top bar's row (kritarc: androidToolboxRowArranged);
   later the Toolbox can be dropped next to the top bar again.
   mirror_actions, select_layout and workspaces are moved from the brush
   toolbar to the top bar (mainToolBar); the expanding spacer is hidden, so
   the vertical sliders get the panel's spare height. The image size,
   rotation and zoom items of patch 16 are added at the right end.
6. A round button at the bottom of the panel shows the foreground color.
   Tapping it switches to the Color Sampler tool; after one sample on the
   canvas (release of pen/mouse/touch on the canvas widget) it switches back
   to the previously active tool. Tapping it again cancels; choosing another
   tool by hand also cancels.

Desktop builds are unchanged.

